#adm/daemons/mailmesg.c
remain ({"ruby@eastern stories","annihilator@eastern.stories",})
mesg "BEGIN FORWARDED TEXT:Elon writes:> Title: Re: problem with 20.21 ...> From:  Leto> Date:  Sun Dec 11> > On Sun Dec 11, Elon wrote:> >  > > We are having problem with 20.21 driver running a heavily modified> > TMI-2 lib based on version 1.0.1. Everything works ok.. fixed the> > type checking and stuff like that....> > But the driver crashes often... it'll go like this:> > Be sure to not use saved binaries, since this is not working> in v20.21> It could be some swapped out file is needed again and the mud> crashes because the bin is corrupt. After the crash it boots again> and reloads the same faulty bin which will crash the mud pretty> soon again. After a reboot it might ignore the binaries for some reason?> > Just a guess,> > Leto> > "
